Subject: [PATCH] Do not expect DXC push-constant matrix arrays to fail on FeMe

The isolated DXC configuration passes on the FeMe ICD. Retain the existing expected failures for Clang and other drivers.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 test/Feature/PushConstant/array_of_matrices.test | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/Feature/PushConstant/array_of_matrices.test b/test/Feature/PushConstant/array_of_matrices.test
index f4eb0c9..bd06950 100644
--- a/test/Feature/PushConstant/array_of_matrices.test
+++ b/test/Feature/PushConstant/array_of_matrices.test
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ DescriptorSets:
 # XFAIL: Clang
 #   Clang: matrices support missing.
 #
-# XFAIL: DXC
+# XFAIL: DXC && !FeMe
 #   DXC observed output: [ 1, 3, 2, 4, 5, 7, 6, 8 ]
 #   Bug: https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXShaderCompiler/issues/8080
 
